[{"sha":"c9b51b3a02f3851f9821d5191718652bab97adac","node_id":"C_kwDOM2nIG9oAKGM5YjUxYjNhMDJmMzg1MWY5ODIxZDUxOTE3MTg2NTJiYWI5N2FkYWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Peder Holdgaard Pedersen","email":"127606677+PederHP@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-11-06T15:57:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-11-06T15:57:15Z"},"message":"fix(schema): restore optional _meta on input requests and responses (#3469)\n\nSEP-2322 stopped these types from being standalone JSON-RPC messages:\nthe request params no longer extend TaskAugmentedRequestParams\n(3443ffac) and the results no longer extend Result (2d37d9de). Both\nbase types carried `_meta`, so it was dropped as a side effect from\nCreateMessageRequestParams, ElicitRequestFormParams,\nElicitRequestURLParams, ElicitResult and ListRootsResult.\n\nListRootsRequest was later given `params?: { _meta?: MetaObject }`\n\"matching other server-initiated input requests\" (d4854bce), but the\nothers never had it. Add the same optional `_meta?: MetaObject` to each.\nRequestParams/Result are not reused because their `_meta` types carry\nrequired client-request and result-level fields that don't apply to\nembedded input requests and responses.\n\nCreateMessageResult is unchanged: it still has `_meta` via\nSamplingMessage.\n\nFixes #3468\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MqPQYRWhLmScrZ19A8eKJp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Sambhav Kothari <skothari44@bloomberg.net>","tree":{"sha":"a240b47e20674f77ea7aebf02389b740c0bb209f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/trees/a240b47e20674f77ea7aebf02389b740c0bb209f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/commits/c9b51b3a02f3851f9821d5191718652bab97adac","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq7fjbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzWgQAJrH6EDzgZrDt07lzlSohaET\nLtUeoUbZOcGUKyNkgKIYC+lMbl/9E6JhWuO08SRg05dv7xVIuJlXUXp56MRHDOFV\nOTVbkG78hPFKjeAv5oBuC9gG7TTQdVFUPbsb6fd7I0mQI4CHTI6jm/epCCHljajN\nKnFJcmP5X869Xn9RBK4Fns28G35gMzhY3GYS11jD0eyqwv7LxUicr+rBhKyzHa9U\npy3Ho00IZzBojXMCcmF6nKz54lbYGCSZl1Ixs2T576hfjyqpocjqG3OLDFh28uM0\nARPk7H84l5Uc3R2+iFPuB0zpFyV3OYAHe3w4lMKs9uT4aL8V85jlfpJYX2r2K9Qg\nbXamxyZ1833r1QXEVPNXOvCweT9mqfhZBWloRuRWU6UQaOS6NO0HIYo6R/7ahXhW\nFiiuVh6kS7DLu8vb2pWyEuT2aOpglgdOF3pjM5/eN5G38WK591VU0+FR+Qae9Fnz\ngxLS2+ER0+vZsIJ5lQznV8i+znlHBy6MXd8Ni4tjGF9uPfL4eqldOpBVCMJOfnGf\nb5jMfkL2PjShip8l0FxUjKmGGD7r6hUHZmiXTmF8vftdJou6q6zpse78dZz2cXjC\nSf+IhHmKMGjU/RuGlAk7LBcIGxmI/MCPHf/AinVuIYZkP2nW+zkApN+asqo/5LaF\nV9EMIY0K/eTameIZJGA6\n=LjFe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a240b47e20674f77ea7aebf02389b740c0bb209f\nparent 38353251fab3bdeead03dd8283b9e66076ce1a7f\nauthor Peder Holdgaard Pedersen <127606677+PederHP@users.noreply.github.com> 1793980635 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1793980635 +0100\n\nfix(schema): restore optional _meta on input requests and responses (#3469)\n\nSEP-2322 stopped these types from being standalone JSON-RPC messages:\nthe request params no longer extend TaskAugmentedRequestParams\n(3443ffac) and the results no longer extend Result (2d37d9de). Both\nbase types carried `_meta`, so it was dropped as a side effect from\nCreateMessageRequestParams, ElicitRequestFormParams,\nElicitRequestURLParams, ElicitResult and ListRootsResult.\n\nListRootsRequest was later given `params?: { _meta?: MetaObject }`\n\"matching other server-initiated input requests\" (d4854bce), but the\nothers never had it. Add the same optional `_meta?: MetaObject` to each.\nRequestParams/Result are not reused because their `_meta` types carry\nrequired client-request and result-level fields that don't apply to\nembedded input requests and responses.\n\nCreateMessageResult is unchanged: it still has `_meta` via\nSamplingMessage.\n\nFixes #3468\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MqPQYRWhLmScrZ19A8eKJp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Sambhav Kothari <skothari44@bloomberg.net>","verified_at":"2026-11-06T15:57:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/commits/c9b51b3a02f3851f9821d5191718652bab97adac","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/commit/c9b51b3a02f3851f9821d5191718652bab97adac","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/commits/c9b51b3a02f3851f9821d5191718652bab97adac/comments","author":{"login":"PederHP","id":127606677,"node_id":"U_kgDOB5sflQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127606677?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PederHP","html_url":"https://github.com/PederHP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PederHP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PederHP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PederHP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PederHP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PederHP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PederHP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PederHP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PederHP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PederHP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"38353251fab3bdeead03dd8283b9e66076ce1a7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/commits/38353251fab3bdeead03dd8283b9e66076ce1a7f","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/commit/38353251fab3bdeead03dd8283b9e66076ce1a7f"}]},{"sha":"38353251fab3bdeead03dd8283b9e66076ce1a7f","node_id":"C_kwDOM2nIG9oAKDM4MzUzMjUxZmFiM2JkZWVhZDAzZGQ4MjgzYjllNjYwNzZjZTFhN2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ola Hungerford","email":"olahungerford@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-06T14:45:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-11-06T14:45:22Z"},"message":"fix(schema): close oneOf type-check bypass and render SEP-2106 Tool examples (#3185)\n\n* fix(schema): close type-check bypass in composition inputSchema example\n\nThe `find_resource` example distinguished its `oneOf` branches with\nbranch-local `properties`. Failing a branch on a type error is exactly\nwhat makes `oneOf` succeed, so a wrongly-typed value in the inactive\nbranch was accepted:\n\n  {\"id\": \"r1\", \"name\": 123}    validated\n  {\"id\": 123, \"name\": \"alpha\"} validated\n\nThe mutual exclusivity the example demonstrates was therefore bypassable\nby supplying both fields and malforming one, and neither field was\ntype-checked while it was the non-selected branch.\n\nHoist `properties` to the schema root and reduce `oneOf` to the\nexclusivity assertion. Validation is otherwise unchanged: `{}` and\n`{id, name}` are still rejected, each field alone still passes. The root\n`properties` map is also no longer empty, so consumers that build a\nparameter list from `inputSchema.properties` advertise the tool's\narguments instead of showing none.\n\nApplied to both draft and 2026-07-28. The 2026-07-28 copy is not\nreferenced by any `@includeCode`, so that revision's rendered schema page\nis unchanged.\n\nAlso wire the two SEP-2106 examples into the draft `Tool` docs. Both were\nadded as files but never referenced, so neither appeared on the rendered\npage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(schema): render SEP-2106 Tool examples in 2026-07-28\n\nThe composition and array-output-schema examples shipped with SEP-2106\nbut were never referenced by an `@includeCode`, so they did not appear\non the rendered Tool page for the current protocol version. Wire both\nin, matching the ordering already applied to draft, and regenerate\ndocs/specification/2026-07-28/schema.mdx.\n\nThe Tool doc-comment blocks in schema/2026-07-28/schema.ts and\nschema/draft/schema.ts are now identical. 2026-07-28 is the Current\nrevision, which per the versioning policy may receive backwards\ncompatible changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(schema): note the composition authoring pitfall on inputSchema\n\nThe inputSchema documentation grants composition keywords but does not\nsay how to use them safely. A subschema that fails on a type error is\nindistinguishable from one that does not apply, so type constraints\nwritten inside `oneOf` branches are skipped for whichever branch does\nnot match -- the bug this PR fixes in the `find_resource` example.\n\nAdd two sentences to the paragraph that grants composition, so the\ncaveat arrives with the permission. Non-normative: the bypassable\npattern is legal JSON Schema, just rarely what the author meant.\n\nApplied to draft and 2026-07-28, with both schema.mdx regenerated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(schema): regenerate schema.json for the inputSchema description\n\nDoc-comment prose feeds the generated `description`, so the composition\nnote requires schema.json to be regenerated for draft and 2026-07-28.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9d7b7fc1986ec590e3789c74422ecc97da7be31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/trees/e9d7b7fc1986ec590e3789c74422ecc97da7be31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/commits/38353251fab3bdeead03dd8283b9e66076ce1a7f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq7egDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf6kQALA2JNXaNcV/EIhEHWE+rOSr\nIQAmTD2ilnR6zwXMddUambzKZWQzY79YMqDkUkJksK+DW4gdrG/bYLm6ZgoBQ2Yt\nLSD9X1vm+rXpOAbeV5itTnxSVHD0WSaeP6N2SuTCRqgThZt6pUbEYt/QCcijTWR7\nEh6YG6P6YLOBMzT4OKWQrH6IiGNJBR13u6pPKosOEHexm6DXCIQlzZBLRLWz180K\nNYR5l/q9wf8RuYbSBEJSdAEqHe8kwSoOQqSr8s1dwlT95jYkinifNL528w87uV+/\nYiJji4NXe9F/HiuLqHDXfe3J01/1pkeONJB7QSeDRNl4RfTwE3pCPg8J4Pi8Xa6s\neR5dZCqvn4aLs0aZBOqbvgvyf2t1yNwDdUy3IXcW3dbvHREN+7S9Y0rIWQcy5A6a\nkefg+3RKHb4nHHVoEUyszX8WVCHBik1uPoALqcIH2J0eh24XjBGZL2uSdES0Jxzk\nJFiu9CK5VIT7k0VhMvzP5a+9fOdTqu0L9+T/azNMZoUD/B5o4P3p5tofOJcwoWXX\no+OD9qFOO2RJgvhb5l0tirODmNKGdoQNYVlhpWMjYPV+IbeIcI+f94zhNjutOWh6\nNGfq05QfSVxivSH4XxMSvllU0t/gWMswodZLTKhAT0bHe/t6iAwcooVkIfu4hM2s\nT62Wa9KHj4xTWtRpkM7G\n=MQBD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e9d7b7fc1986ec590e3789c74422ecc97da7be31\nparent 22bb5b965a58e7f502deb184b51a8a4b8bf6067a\nauthor Ola Hungerford <olahungerford@gmail.com> 1793976322 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1793976322 +0000\n\nfix(schema): close oneOf type-check bypass and render SEP-2106 Tool examples (#3185)\n\n* fix(schema): close type-check bypass in composition inputSchema example\n\nThe `find_resource` example distinguished its `oneOf` branches with\nbranch-local `properties`. Failing a branch on a type error is exactly\nwhat makes `oneOf` succeed, so a wrongly-typed value in the inactive\nbranch was accepted:\n\n  {\"id\": \"r1\", \"name\": 123}    validated\n  {\"id\": 123, \"name\": \"alpha\"} validated\n\nThe mutual exclusivity the example demonstrates was therefore bypassable\nby supplying both fields and malforming one, and neither field was\ntype-checked while it was the non-selected branch.\n\nHoist `properties` to the schema root and reduce `oneOf` to the\nexclusivity assertion. Validation is otherwise unchanged: `{}` and\n`{id, name}` are still rejected, each field alone still passes. The root\n`properties` map is also no longer empty, so consumers that build a\nparameter list from `inputSchema.properties` advertise the tool's\narguments instead of showing none.\n\nApplied to both draft and 2026-07-28. The 2026-07-28 copy is not\nreferenced by any `@includeCode`, so that revision's rendered schema page\nis unchanged.\n\nAlso wire the two SEP-2106 examples into the draft `Tool` docs. Both were\nadded as files but never referenced, so neither appeared on the rendered\npage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(schema): render SEP-2106 Tool examples in 2026-07-28\n\nThe composition and array-output-schema examples shipped with SEP-2106\nbut were never referenced by an `@includeCode`, so they did not appear\non the rendered Tool page for the current protocol version. Wire both\nin, matching the ordering already applied to draft, and regenerate\ndocs/specification/2026-07-28/schema.mdx.\n\nThe Tool doc-comment blocks in schema/2026-07-28/schema.ts and\nschema/draft/schema.ts are now identical. 2026-07-28 is the Current\nrevision, which per the versioning policy may receive backwards\ncompatible changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(schema): note the composition authoring pitfall on inputSchema\n\nThe inputSchema documentation grants composition keywords but does not\nsay how to use them safely. A subschema that fails on a type error is\nindistinguishable from one that does not apply, so type constraints\nwritten inside `oneOf` branches are skipped for whichever branch does\nnot match -- the bug this PR fixes in the `find_resource` example.\n\nAdd two sentences to the paragraph that grants composition, so the\ncaveat arrives with the permission. Non-normative: the bypassable\npattern is legal JSON Schema, just rarely what the author meant.\n\nApplied to draft and 2026-07-28, with both schema.mdx regenerated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(schema): regenerate schema.json for the inputSchema description\n\nDoc-comment prose feeds the generated `description`, so the composition\nnote requires schema.json to be regenerated for draft and 2026-07-28.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-11-06T14:45:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/commits/38353251fab3bdeead03dd8283b9e66076ce1a7f","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/commit/38353251fab3bdeead03dd8283b9e66076ce1a7f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/commits/38353251fab3bdeead03dd8283b9e66076ce1a7f/comments","author":{"login":"olaservo","id":16480113,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDgwMTEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16480113?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olaservo","html_url":"https://github.com/olaservo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olaservo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olaservo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olaservo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olaservo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"htt